      ":question/id": "2dcc0dd6-aca0-5064-9dc8-0e3932c2fd83",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the real numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none of the sets apply, select \"None of the above\".",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{N}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. For instance, $\\frac{1}{2}$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Z}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ contains the negative rational numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\nTherefore, select \"None of the above\".",
